## Lore

Cyborg troops play a strong role in the Quebec Army and are another example of
Free Quebec''s preference for powerful, one-man units ' || char(8212) || ' cyborgs, Juicers, Glitter
Boys, SAMAS ' || char(8212) || ' roughly man-sized soldiers who can move and function alone or in a
small squad while each packing the firepower of a whole squad of ordinary human
infantry.

Cyborg soldiers provide sustaining fire with medium to heavy weapons, lead
infantry charges, hold ground against assault, give Glitter Boys close-range
support, and run small squad reconnaissance, deep wilderness recce, seek and
destroy, rescue and Special Operations. On the offensive they follow the Glitter
Boys and fire on aerial targets and enemy flankers, then open up in concert once
in range. The firepower of a battalion of Cyborg Shock Troopers can rival that
of the Glitter Boys.

Partial and full conversion cyborgs are an important part of the army, with over
55% serving as career soldiers, and Quebec uses the same programs for service,
retirement and decommissioning as the Coalition States ' || char(8212) || ' most of which the
Coalition in fact adopted from Free Quebec. Roughly a third of the police are
partial cyborgs and 18% are full conversion; in wartime the police are the core
of civil defense.

Any human with the spirit to fight and good mental health may volunteer.

## GM Notes

**Every cyborg soldier is fitted with amplified hearing and a sound filtration
system**, to filter out the noise of combat and to buffer the sonic booms of the
Boom Guns. They suffer no combat penalty even standing right next to a Glitter
Boy.

The cyborgs are the work of **The Liberty Reserve**, a covert division of the
Quebec Military formed in 99 P.A. in direct defiance of the Chi-Town agreement,
responsible for designing and maintaining the nation''s human augmentation
programs. Its existence had to be kept secret: R&D of this kind was reserved
exclusively for Chi-Town.

Standard military issue is all the appropriate ammunition and equipment for the
''Borg''s body styling and weapon systems, an energy rifle of choice, four extra
E-Clips, four grenades of choice, utility belt, backpack, a walkie-talkie for
back-up, and regular maintenance and repairs. Available on assignment: jet pack,
hover vehicle or other transport, rail gun, and additional weapons and equipment.
The character has medium security clearance to most Free Quebec military bases,
hospitals and facilities.

Additional bionics and cybernetics may be added to both partial and full
conversion ''Borgs as a reward or for a special mission, drawn from Rifts, Rifts
Triax and the NGR, or Rifts Underseas. Unique and variant cyborgs are specially
constructed for officers and Special Forces.

Standard military ranking, private to general.
', 'published', 'data-script'
